# CivicCast License Notice

CivicCast is a dual-licensed open-source project. Different parts of this repository are released under different licenses, each chosen for the kind of artifact it covers.

## Code

All source code in this repository — Python modules, JavaScript / TypeScript modules, build scripts, configuration files, and CI workflows — is licensed under the **Apache License, Version 2.0**.

The full text is in [LICENSE-CODE](LICENSE-CODE).

Every source file carries the SPDX header:

```
# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
# Copyright (c) The CivicCast Authors
```

## Documentation

All documentation in this repository — Markdown files in `docs/`, the README, CONTRIBUTING, SECURITY, SUPPORT, CODE_OF_CONDUCT, CHANGELOG, ADRs, the spec, the release plan, templates, and any prose-format files outside source code — is licensed under the **Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License (CC BY 4.0)**.

The full text is in [LICENSE-DOCS](LICENSE-DOCS).

## Why dual-licensed

Apache 2.0 is the right license for the executable artifact: it is permissive, patent-protective, widely accepted by municipal procurement and nonprofit governance, and compatible with redistribution by downstream packagers.

CC BY 4.0 is the right license for the documentation: it explicitly contemplates non-software content, encourages reuse with attribution, and is the standard choice for public-good documentation that operators may need to fork into their own internal docs, training materials, or board-meeting handouts.

## Contributions

Contributions are accepted under the [Developer Certificate of Origin](https://developercertificate.org/) — see [CONTRIBUTING.md](CONTRIBUTING.md). By signing off on a commit, you agree your code is licensed under Apache 2.0 and your documentation under CC BY 4.0.

## Trademark

"CivicCast" is the project name. Trademark policy will be added before the public 1.0 release. Until then, please attribute clearly when using the name in derived works.

## Third-party components

Third-party components included in this repository (or required at install time) retain their own licenses. See the [`pyproject.toml`](pyproject.toml) and the per-module dependency lists for the canonical inventory once Sprint 0.1 establishes the dependency graph.
